1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Hi, we're team ___, for the
Lunar Landing Site Navigator challenge.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,000
At the Moon's south pole, the Sun skims the horizon.
A lander needs sunlight for power and a view of Earth to call home.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This is CLPS Lunar Mission Browser.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,500
Pick a landing date and up to three sites.
It shows sunlight, Earth time, the longest night, and a verdict,

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,000
all from NASA JPL ephemeris data,
checked against JPL Horizons.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Students can press "Explain it to me".

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Faster, clearer landing choices, for planners
and for everyone curious about the Moon.
